String:Collection of characters.
Methods:
1.length()=returns the number of characters in a string.
String s="java";
System.out.println(s.length());
output=4

2.charAt()=returns the character at a specified index.
String s="java";
System.out.println(s.chatAt(1));
output='a'

3.toUpperCase()=converts all characters into uppercase.
String s="java";
System.out.println(s.toUppercase());
output="JAVA"

4.toLowerscase()=convert all characters into lowercase.
String s="JAVA";
System.out.println(s.toLowercase());
output="java"

5.equalsIgnoreCase()=compares strings without considering uppercase or lowercase differences.
String a="JAVA";
String b="java";
System.out.println(s.equalsIgnorecase());
output:true

6.replace()=replaces characters 

